Z||000006||MinnGreenGT||11-09-2001||04:24 PM||||I've heard that the Aurora V6 (also known as the "ShortStar") <B>would</B> be a good motor for the Fiero.  If you didn't have to engineer so much for the system.  Someone told me that it would take as much work to install the ShortStar as it would the Northstar. You'd spend about the same and end up with less power.  It'd be like buying Archie's V8 kit to intall a 4.3L Vortech V6!  (Really.  The 4.3 would require the same adaptors as a 350)<p>[This message has been edited by MinnGreenGT (edited 11-09-2001).]||||reg||1
